# Android release signing — TEMPLATE (Story 7.6).
#
# Copy this file to `keystore.properties` (same directory: android/) and fill in
# real values to produce a signed release AAB/APK. The real `keystore.properties`
# and the `*.jks`/`*.keystore` it points at are gitignored and MUST NEVER be
# committed. When `keystore.properties` is absent the release build is left
# unsigned and Gradle does not error (dev/CI stay green).
#
# Create a keystore first (see docs/mobile-build.md):
#   keytool -genkey -v -keystore release.jks -alias anglewars \
#           -keyalg RSA -keysize 2048 -validity 10000
#
# storeFile is resolved by build.gradle via file(...), i.e. RELATIVE TO the
# android/app module directory. For a keystore kept OUTSIDE the repo (recommended),
# use an ABSOLUTE path here, e.g. storeFile=/home/you/keys/anglewars-release.jks
# (the absolute placeholder below is a stand-in for exactly that). A bare relative
# name like storeFile=release.jks would be looked up under android/app/, not the
# android/ directory this file lives in — so only use a relative name if the .jks
# actually sits in android/app/.

storeFile=/absolute/path/to/anglewars-release.jks
storePassword=CHANGE_ME
keyAlias=anglewars
keyPassword=CHANGE_ME
